{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1392138-imprisoning-an-avatar","id":1392138,"title":"Imprisoning An Avatar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-28T00:18:00-07:00","id":1392138,"title":"Imprisoning An Avatar","content":"Could a mage imprison an Avatar at the time of another's mage death? For instance, binding the Avatar in a reliquary, so that it would not reincarnate. That would make sense against Nephandic Avatars. If magick can destroy by Gilgul an Avatar, why not imprison it? Assuming a mage's Paradigm allows it (and I would say Tradition Paradigms all could), what Spheres would be necessary? Spirit 5, Prime 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T06:04:58-07:00","id":1392176,"title":"","content":"I would think so. It would be much like making a Philactery. At least Spirit 5 &amp; Prime 5 would be needed to create the receptacle and bind the Avatar, yes.<br /> <br /> This won't prevent every aspect of reincarnation, though, as mages with Philacteries can still connect with their fated Avatars - but I think the owner could be safe from the corruption 'til the item is found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T06:29:37-07:00","id":1392180,"title":"","content":"That sounds about right. How about adding correspondence to banish it into a prison dimension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T15:19:02-07:00","id":1392328,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest problem with any such attempt would be simple: making it permanent enough to matter.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons Gilgul works (for a definition of works) is because it's &quot;damage.&quot; Destroying something doesn't cause it to automatically repair itself upon the duration of a spell wearing off.<br /> <br /> Trying to trap an Avatar indefinitely upon the target's death would be difficult, unless you're planning on ritually killing them, on ensuring a powerful enough effect for such a thing.<br /> <br /> And even then you have the psychopomps and the target avatar that would actively be fighting against such things (plus and Nephandi that might want to sabotage such efforts on general principle to force the Tradtions into the hypocrisy of Gilgul as their only option). Gnawing away at the spell to bind them until it can't hold them in might take years but... so what in the eyes of such entities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T05:34:21-07:00","id":1392483,"title":"","content":"Well, what I ever say about &quot;everlasting seals&quot;: They're permanent until the plot comes, and then they break.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be fun to have an easy solution against Nephandy, that would avoid the whole drama.<br /> <br /> Gilgul it's the more permanent, recommended solution (the Ascencion Warrior would disgress, but he's an exception and maybe a fraud), but this could still be a reasonable choice for wizards that shy of killing souls (well, better than just killing the Nephandi).<br /> <br /> I can see a wizard doing that to keep the Nephandi from reincarnating &quot;until I find a way to cure the inversion&quot; (most likely never - but what's Mage without unrealistic hopes?). I think it can be good food for plots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-29-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:55:06-07:00","id":1392500,"title":"","content":"Besides, the mage might be storing the Avatar for study rather than any other reason, perhaps so as to figure out how to create their own version of an altered Avatar. &quot;Let's make a celestial version of these abyssal thingies&quot; for example... Go go hubris!<br /> <br /> Imagine a mage who has killed maybe a few hundred nephandi and stored their avatars away for just such a purpose. Maybe he's even made a few modified avatars already... Or an artificial one. Then he or she dies. Within a decade, the magick sustaining these things will fail. The NPCs happen upon this Mage's person's journal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:55:04-07:00","id":1392557,"title":"","content":"Bah, just shunt that avatar 500 years into the future.<br /> <br /> ..just...don't do that with all the Nephandic avatars, or the plot becomes <i>&quot;Holy sh$7 why is there a sudden population explosion of Nephandi??&quot;</i> at some point in time. Like...for example, now. That would be an interesting plot as well &gt;_&gt;<br /> And then a brave troupe of Mages travels into the past to try and stop that from ever happening...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-30-2020, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T20:48:30-07:00","id":1392740,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for the responses, some nice idea brainstorming here. I particularly like the Philactery suggestion.<br /> <br /> In Book of Secrets creating a Philactery demands Correspondence 5, Prime 5, Spirit 5 plus Mind 4 and Matter 4 to do it to oneself in a object. I guess doing it to another dying mage's Avatar would no need Mind 4, no? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>, what did you mean by &quot;mages with Philacteries can still connect with their fated Avatars&quot; and about every aspect of reincarnation bit?<br /> <br /> Also, do you all think psychopomps would intervene to liberate the Avatars? Are they even active beyond the Mythic Age?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T21:01:53-07:00","id":1392743,"title":"","content":"Sometimes people are born who must connect (find and be in the presence of and/or touch/gain control of their avatars to become mages, and sometimes these avatars are in the form of a material thing, such as the aforementioned phylactery. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't be too worried about psychopomps if I had enough spheres to bind an Avatar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T06:12:08-07:00","id":1393403,"title":"","content":"That. I always interpreted that not all mages with the Philactery defect had a spell casted on them, some people are born with their Avatar being inside a material thing. In any case, a mage with a philcatery isn't actually &quot;souless&quot;, it just has to connect with the Philactery to get magick (which, btw, can't be done by other people) - thus other, subtler, aspects of the soul must be present that allow such communion.<br /> <br /> And as for needing Mind: That depends on how much do you think the Avatar relates to the Mind Sphere. It's not unreasonable to think that the Avatar it's partially a psychological construct. How much of your soul it's Mind? - I think the ST has to decide such a thing. I would make it Prime/Spirit minimum. Correspondence to create a Ward-like effect can be argued for, as can be Mind. Matter only if it's desired to reinforce the receptacle against phisical punishment (which it's very advantageous, but not necessary)<br /> <br /> Psychopomps may be active or not, but once their influence it's named anything goes: Gilgul it's not a safe way to eradicate Nephandi either, as Psychopomps may be able to restore a shred Avatar. In general, they do *not* act - they're one of the most misterious entities of Revised. And mages ain't going to be worried about them. Among other things, because most mages don't know anything about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-01-2020, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T02:45:35-07:00","id":1393600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1392138-imprisoning-an-avatar?p=1392740#post1392740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are they even active beyond the Mythic Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, unless your chronicle is set in a timeline with the imminent end of the world looming over everything.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}